WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.410
The Red Room gave an orphaned girl the deadly
skills that turned her into the Black Widow,

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.690
and it took one of America's most patriotic
heroes and brainwashed him into becoming the

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.450
lethal Winter Soldier.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:16.129
For the twisted history of the Red Room, though,
those two characters are only the beginning.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:21.820
In the continuity of the comics, the Red Room
dates back to at least World War II.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.580
Here in the real world, though, the Red Room
didn't make its first appearance until the

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:30.090
late ‘90s, which is pretty surprising when
you consider that Black Widow, its most famous

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:34.850
student, had been a major character in the
Avengers for about 30 years at that point.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:39.460
Before "Shadows &amp; Light #1" hit the shelves
with a story that expanded on Natasha's true

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.460
past, Black Widow's origin was relatively
simple, at least by comic book standards.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.789
Before she was a superhero, she was a supervillain
— she fought Iron Man back in her first

00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:54.309
appearance — and before that, she was just
Natalia Romanova (aka Natasha Romanoff), the

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:58.870
star ballerina in the world-famous Bolshoi
Ballet and married to a military pilot named

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.370
Alexi Shostakov.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:05.180
When Alexi died in the line of duty, Natalia
signed up with the KGB, using her finely honed

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.189
physical skills and a knack for martial arts
to train as an assassin.

00:01:09.189 --> 00:01:13.030
She took the name Black Widow because she
somehow knew that Americans were terrified

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:16.640
of spiders, and because, you know, she was
literally a widow.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.530
Except that she wasn't.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.150
For one thing, Alexi had never actually died.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:25.460
The KGB had faked his death to turn him into
the Red Guardian, the Soviet counterpart of

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:26.649
Captain America.

00:01:26.649 --> 00:01:31.270
That made things pretty awkward the first
time he was reunited with his wife, a not-so-happy

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:35.869
event that came when he fought both Black
Widow and her new boyfriend, Hawkeye.

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:39.340
Another misleading thing about Black Widow's
original backstory is that it later turned

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.380
out that Natalia had never actually been a
ballerina.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:47.009
Those were false memories implanted during
her training, leaving us with a pretty compelling

00:01:47.009 --> 00:01:51.249
question: If that wasn't actually Black Widow's
origin, what was?

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:57.539
One of the more interesting pieces of the
Red Room puzzle came in Uncanny X-Men #268.

00:01:57.539 --> 00:02:02.329
The story is a team-up starring Wolverine
that takes place in two different eras.

00:02:02.329 --> 00:02:06.649
One half of the story happens in the present
day of 1990, when Wolverine and Black Widow

00:02:06.649 --> 00:02:10.950
team up to take on the evil ninjas of the
Hand, who are stirring up trouble in Madripoor.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:15.890
The second half of the story takes place 49
years earlier, in 1941, when Wolvie teams

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.390
up with Captain America to, well, also fight
the Hand.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.870
Back then, however, there was one more wrinkle
to the story.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.700
The trouble being stirred up was in the form
of a young girl that was kidnapped from Moscow

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.140
by Baron Strucker.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.140
Her name?

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.760
Natalia Romanova, the girl who would grow
up to be the Black Widow.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.920
If you've been paying attention to the dates,
you might've already caught on to a pretty

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.060
notable quirk to this story.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:45.410
The Widow was a young girl — somewhere around
ten years old judging by the art — in 1941,

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.960
and she was still out there fighting bad guys
as an Avenger 50 years later, looking like

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:53.030
she was maybe in her early 30s at most.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:57.250
That's not all that unusual in the Marvel
Universe, but unlike the characters with whom

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:01.450
she shared that story, the Widow doesn't have
a mutant healing factor, and she didn't spend

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.750
years frozen in a block of ice to explain
the apparent discrepancy.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:10.410
Dancers tend to age pretty gracefully, but
there was clearly something more going on

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.520
with her backstory to explain her lasting
youth.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.420
Unlike most of Marvel's main characters, Black
Widow doesn't actually have a definitive,

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.430
set-in-stone origin story.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.890
That's especially odd when you consider that
they literally published a comic called Black

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:29.090
Widow: Deadly Origin back in 2010.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:34.340
She's maintained an air of mystery for over
50 years, largely because her training involved

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.010
the Red Room altering her memories to suit
their own sinister purposes.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.220
The facts go a little something like this.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:45.840
In 1928, baby Natalia was rescued from a burning
building in Stalingrad by Ivan Petrovich.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.590
Ivan was told by Natalia's previous caretaker
that li'l Natalia was "a Romanoff," a name

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:55.690
which naturally hinted at a possible connection
to Russia's lost royal family, who were seemingly

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:59.400
all executed ten years prior in the Russian
Revolution.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.520
That connection, however, would never be fully
explored.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:07.750
Instead, despite Ivan's protests, Natalia
was declared an orphan in 1940, and on the

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:11.720
order of Joseph Stalin himself, sent to a
new training facility where she proved to

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:16.810
be so adept at learning to kill that the Hand
tried to steal her away and Wolverine had

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:17.810
to get involved.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:23.280
The weird thing is, despite his well-chronicled
tendency to adopt young women as a surrogate

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:28.330
father figure, he left her in the care of
the KGB ... along with her 27 "sisters."

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:35.320
While she would become its most successful
product, Natalia Romanova was certainly not

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:39.570
the only young girl trained in the deadly
arts of assassination by the Red Room and

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.930
its masters in the Soviet Union's sinister
Department X.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:49.120
Instead, she was one of 28 "students," aka
Widows, all of whom were orphaned girls who

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:52.660
had the falsified memories of being dancers
for the Bolshoi Ballet.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:57.080
The architect of this brainwashing was Department
X's leader, Vasily Karpov.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:02.500
Under his direction, Department X recruited
a "psychotechnologist" named Grigor Pchelintsov,

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.710
who'd invented the technique of implanting
false memories.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:09.770
Together with a "programmer" known only as
"Professor Radchenko," who later defected

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:13.990
to the United States, he implanted the Red
Room's students with their false memories,

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:19.040
designed to turn the girls into sleeper agents
who could pass undetected in other countries.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.430
Unfortunately, there was a pretty big flaw
in the program.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:27.760
The process itself was torturous, and the
results weren't quite as undetectable as they

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.740
wanted, especially since the conflicting memories
would sometimes try to assert themselves at

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:36.580
the same time, leading to the Widows giving
multiple answers to the same question.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.639
The mental modifications weren't the only
ones, though.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:44.930
The Red Room's staff also featured Lyudmila
Kudrin, a chemical scientist and geneticist.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:49.950
Her work resulted in the drug treatments that
gave Black Widow her unnaturally long lifespan,

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:54.010
as well as causing a biological response that
would prevent the women of the Red Room from

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:57.889
ever giving birth because "we wanted warriors,
not mothers."

00:05:57.889 --> 00:06:02.210
She also designed a pheromone treatment to
keep the trainees docile, programming them

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.560
to be unable to attack their superiors should
they ever get the urge to rebel.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:11.720
There was another notable member of the Red
Room's faculty, although calling him a member

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.920
of the staff is pushing it.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:18.440
He was another one of Comrade Karpov's pet
projects, and he was responsible for putting

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.710
Natalia and the others through a vicious round
of advanced combat training.

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:26.530
He was a pretty effective teacher, too, although
that's to be expected.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.570
After all, he learned to fight from Captain
America.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:34.330
His name, of course, was James Buchanan Barnes,
better known at the time as the Winter Soldier.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:39.880
Karpov was the one who'd fished Bucky out
of the ocean after his presumed death in 1945.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:44.200
Using the same technology that he'd employed
to implant false memories into the Black Widows,

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:49.440
he erased Bucky's old patriotic personality
and turned him into a mindless, ultra-efficient

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:50.440
killing machine.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:56.280
While both were under the purview of Department
X, the Winter Soldier program and the Red

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:00.490
Room were kept separate, with Bucky's side
gig as a combat instructor being their only

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:01.920
real crossover.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.260
There's a reason for that, too.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:06.160
The Red Room was focused exclusively on women.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.080
Except, of course, for the one time that it
wasn't.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:13.930
For a brief period, the Red Room experimented
with a counterpart to the Black Widow program

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:15.310
involving boys.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:20.340
In keeping with the arachnid naming convention,
these agents were code-named "Wolf Spiders,"

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:23.530
and they received similar training and conditioning.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:27.440
Considering that the Red Room's most prominent
graduate wound up defecting to America where

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:31.530
she joined both S.H.I.E.L.D. and the Avengers,
it might surprise you to learn that the Wolf

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:34.760
Spider program was apparently even less successful.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:39.790
The Wolf Spider program only produced a single
graduate: Niko Constantin.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:43.930
Rather than send him on missions, the Russian
government simply scrapped the project and

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:48.620
sent Niko to a Siberian gulag where they dumped
all of their super-powered problems.

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:53.360
It was there, decades later, that he crossed
paths with Bucky, who'd trained him as well.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:58.520
The exact circumstances of his dismissal were
never actually revealed other than Bucky mentioning

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:03.770
that he was "psychotic" after his conditioning,
but it was established that unlike the Black

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:07.120
Widows, he never got the chemical treatment
that slowed his aging.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:12.820
One of the most notable other graduates of
the Red Room was Yelena Belova.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:16.810
The big difference this time around, though,
was that Yelena didn't go through the mental

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:19.100
conditioning that her predecessor had.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.790
Instead, her fanatical devotion to the cause
came naturally.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:27.870
On paper, her scores exceeded Natasha's, and
her training cultivated a talent for spycraft

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:32.149
and assassination, honing her into a living
weapon to the point where she was officially

00:08:32.149 --> 00:08:34.039
given the "Black Widow" code name.

00:08:34.039 --> 00:08:38.669
Needless to say, this brought her into a conflict
with her predecessor as she attempted to take

00:08:38.669 --> 00:08:40.459
her place permanently.

00:08:40.459 --> 00:08:44.800
The irony was not only that Yelena would never
be the only Black Widow, but that she wasn't

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.610
even the only Yelena Belova.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:51.050
In an effort to cut through the time-consuming
process of rounding up athletic orphans, the

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:56.069
Red Room began embarking on a new tactic — cloning
their best operatives and just programming

00:08:56.069 --> 00:09:00.399
their brains directly rather than overwriting
existing memories.

00:09:00.399 --> 00:09:04.860
After discovering the truth about her own
origin, a clone of Natasha that had activated

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:08.930
after the genuine article's apparent death
began to work against the program.

00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:13.950
The Natasha clone began to use the Yelena
clones for her own purposes, and in the ultimate

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:18.320
insult, she killed the real Yelena in the
process to make things easier.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:19.320
It even happened off-panel.

00:09:20.839 --> 00:09:25.129
One of the more recent graduates of the Red
Room is Nadia van Dyne, whose origin story

00:09:25.129 --> 00:09:29.180
reveals that if the Red Room couldn't find
enough orphans to train, they'd just make

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.350
a few of their own.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:35.070
Nadia is the daughter of Hank Pym — the
original Ant-Man — and Maria Trovaya, his

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:39.889
first wife, who was introduced in a flashback
all the way back in 1963.

00:09:39.889 --> 00:09:43.410
In that story, it was revealed that she'd
been kidnapped and killed on their honeymoon,

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:47.139
leaving Hank understandably enraged and heartbroken.

00:09:47.139 --> 00:09:51.259
Over 50 years later, it was revealed that
Maria's kidnapping was faked, and that she'd

00:09:51.259 --> 00:09:55.019
stayed alive long enough to give birth to
her daughter, Nadia, who was given to the

00:09:55.019 --> 00:09:57.320
Red Room as their latest project.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:02.420
Nadia had apparently inherited her father's
genius, and the Red Room leaned into that.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:07.179
Rather than simply manufacturing a super spy,
Nadia's branch of the Red Room was focused

00:10:07.179 --> 00:10:12.790
on an attempt to essentially create mad scientists,
hoping to control the next generation of minds

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:17.269
brilliant enough to do things like build Iron
Man armor or time machines.

00:10:17.269 --> 00:10:21.879
To that end, the Red Room's trainers encouraged
Nadia by revealing her parentage.

00:10:21.879 --> 00:10:26.279
Unfortunately for them, telling Nadia about
her famous American superhero father had the

00:10:26.279 --> 00:10:31.180
side effect of fueling her desire to escape,
which turns out to be pretty easy when you

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:35.429
have access to size-changing Pym Particles
and the brains to use them.

00:10:35.429 --> 00:10:39.550
After her escape, Nadia was mentored by her
stepmother Janet van Dyne, better known as

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:40.720
the Wasp.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:45.259
Inspired and nurtured for the first time by
someone who didn't want to use her brilliance

00:10:45.259 --> 00:10:50.709
for world domination, Nadia took both Janet's
superheroic identity and her last name for

00:10:50.709 --> 00:10:57.319
her own, changing her name Nadia van Dyne
and leaping into action as the all-new Wasp.

00:10:58.319 --> 00:11:02.589
The dreamy hallucination of Age of Ultron
isn't the only time we've seen the Red Room

00:11:02.589 --> 00:11:07.029
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe pre-Black
Widow, and Natasha Romanoff isn't the only

00:11:07.029 --> 00:11:09.899
graduate who's stepped into the spotlight,
either.

00:11:09.899 --> 00:11:14.100
Decades before Nat took her undercover job
as Tony Stark's personal assistant in Iron

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:19.720
Man 2, Agent Peggy Carter crossed paths with
the Red Room prototype, Dottie Underwood.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:24.050
Played by Bridget Regan, Dottie was one of
the primary antagonists of Agent Carter, a

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:27.779
spy who infiltrated Peggy's life in order
to eventually take her out for the Russian

00:11:27.779 --> 00:11:28.939
government.

00:11:28.939 --> 00:11:33.889
Even by the standards of the Red Room, the
glimpses we see of her training were especially

00:11:33.889 --> 00:11:34.889
harsh.

00:11:34.889 --> 00:11:39.939
In 1937, a young Dottie killed her only friend
in a sparring match, ordered by her trainer

00:11:39.939 --> 00:11:43.689
to choke her to death in a promising display
of her lethal talents.

00:11:43.689 --> 00:11:48.649
Needless to say, Dottie wasn't particularly
well-adjusted as an adult, and her fixation

00:11:48.649 --> 00:11:53.509
on Peggy was packed with moments that were
as full of danger as they were of sapphic

00:11:53.509 --> 00:11:54.509
subtext.

00:11:54.509 --> 00:11:58.360
"You don't want this visit on the record,
which means you're probably going behind someone's

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.600
back.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:02.089
… How naughty."

